of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal
in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights
to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell
copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is
furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:
</p><p>
The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all
copies or substantial portions of the Software.
</p><p>
THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
SOFTWARE.
</p>
<h2>Links</h2>
<p class="link"> options_parser, strings</p>
<h2>Globals</h2>
<p class="global"> destination # destination folder</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="global"> include_tests # flag indicating whether test files should be processed</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="global"> output_type # indicate html/vimhelp format</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="global"> separator # directory separator</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="global"> title_page # name of html material to paste into index</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<h2>Procedures</h2>
<p class="procedure">document_all (<i>filelist</i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">document_file (<i>filename</i>)</p>
<p>
Given a file, reads every line in the file and divides comments into
groups: title, procedure, record.
Also collects global, link, procedure and record definitions.
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">get_filename (<i>path</i>)</p>
<p>
Given a pathname, returns the filename only.
</p><p>
<pre>
  get_filename("src/filename.icn") => "filename.icn"
</pre>
</p><p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">get_item_args (<i>line</i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">get_item_name (<i>line, item_name</i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">main (<i>arglist</i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">write_comments_html (<i>f, comments</i>)</p>
<p>
Writes lists of comments in HTML format:
<ul>
<li>blank lines signal a paragraph break</li>
<li>lines starting with '  ' are part of a pre-block</li>
<li>lines starting with '. ' are part of an enumerated list</li>
<li>lines starting with '* ' or '- ' are part of an itemised list</li>
<li>lines with '[word] sentence' are description lists</li>
</ul>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">write_doc_pages_html (<i>doc_data</i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">write_doc_pages_vimhelp (<i>doc_data</i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">write_footer (<i>f</i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">write_header (<i>f, title</i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">write_home_page_html (<i>all_info</i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">write_home_page_vimhelp (<i>doc_data</i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">write_page_html (<i>file, title, info, all_info</i>)</p>
<p>
Write page information in HTML format.
info is an instance of file_doc, containing all documentation on file
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">write_page_vimhelp (<i>filename, title, info, all_info</i>)</p>
<p>
Write page information in vimhelp format.
info is an instance of file_doc, containing all information on file
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">write_sidebar (<i>f, doc_data</i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="procedure">write_version (<i></i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<h2>Records</h2>
<p class="record">file_doc (<i>filename, comments, globals, links, procs, records</i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
<p class="record">item_doc (<i>item_name, comments</i>)</p>
<p>
</p>
<hr>
</div>
